<article class="env-lemma" id="09ZX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09ZX">Lemma <span data-tag="09ZX">76.9.8</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Y \subset Y'$ be a thickening of algebraic spaces over $S$. Let $X' \to Y'$ be a morphism and set $X = Y \times _{Y'} X'$. Then $(X \subset X') \to (Y \subset Y')$ is a morphism of thickenings. If $Y \subset Y'$ is a first (resp. finite order) thickening, then $X \subset X'$ is a first (resp. finite order) thickening. </p>
</article> 
